# Phase 16: copy to infra/Caddyfile and replace api.yourdomain.com with your real domain
# (must have a DNS A/AAAA record pointing at this VM before starting Caddy, or it can't get a
# Let's Encrypt certificate). Caddy handles HTTPS automatically -- no manual certbot/cron needed.
#
# This is what makes RateLimitFilter's X-Forwarded-For read (Phase 15) trustworthy: Caddy sets
# X-Forwarded-For itself for every request it proxies, overwriting anything a client sent, so a
# caller can no longer spoof their own rate-limit bucket. See docs/security.md.

api.yourdomain.com {
	reverse_proxy backend:8080
}
